      "writtenOn": "2026-04-07T17:28:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I agree, but I think it changes the semantics to be that the headroom is the headroom of the whole allocation (or binding chunk), vs. after the last stride-instance. I think that is more intuitive, and is equivalent in the current case where count\u003d1. If that matches your understanding, I think the comment for `getMappedSubrangeWithHeadroom` is slightly out of date.",
      "parentUuid": "240179d9_15e0be69",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 55,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 55,
        "endChar": 60
      },
